# Account session tests: /account/login, /account/me, /account/logout
# Run with the REST Client extension, top to bottom, dev server + dev db already running.
#
# Uses REST Client's cookie jar (rest-client.rememberCookiesForSubsequentRequests, default:
# true) to carry the session cookie from login into the later /me and /logout requests
# automatically, same as a browser would - no manual cookie copying needed.
#
# Re-running the whole file: request 2 (signup) will fail with 409 "already exists" since
# the account is already in the db. Start from request 3 on repeat runs, or change the test
# email below and clear REST Client's cookies (Command Palette > "Rest Client: Clear Cookies")
# for a fully clean slate.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@testName = testuser1
@testEmail = testuser1@example.com
# isValidPhoneNumber() is called with no default country, so this needs full E.164 (leading + and country code)
@testTel = +84901234567
@testPassword = TestPass123!

### 1. GET /account/me - no session yet
# Expect: 200 { "user": null }
GET {{baseUrl}}/account/me

### 2. POST /account/signup - create the account these tests use
# Expect: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "{{testName}}",
    "email": "{{testEmail}}",
    "tel": "{{testTel}}",
    "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### 3. POST /account/login - wrong password
# Expect: 401 { "error": "Invalid email or password" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "{{testEmail}}",
    "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 4. POST /account/login - email that was never signed up
# Expect: 401 { "error": "Invalid email or password" } - same message as #3, doesn't leak
# whether the account exists
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "nobody@example.com",
    "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### 5. POST /account/login - malformed body (password not a string)
# Expect: 400 { "error": "Email and password are required" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "{{testEmail}}",
    "password": 12345
}

### 6. POST /account/login - correct credentials
# Expect: 200 + user object in the body, Set-Cookie header with the session id
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "{{testEmail}}",
    "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### 7. GET /account/me - now with a session cookie
# Expect: 200 { "user": {...} } with the logged-in account's data
GET {{baseUrl}}/account/me

### 8. POST /account/logout - end the session
# Expect: 200 { "user": null }, Set-Cookie clearing the cookie, session row removed from the db
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/logout

### 9. GET /account/me - after logout
# Expect: 200 { "user": null } again - cookie is cleared and/or session no longer exists
GET {{baseUrl}}/account/me

### 10. POST /account/logout - calling logout again with no active session
# Expect: 200 { "user": null }, no 500 - should be a no-op when there's nothing to clear
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/logout
